---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { methods, qmlApi, statusFields } from "../../data/api";
const categories = Array.from(new Set(methods.map(method => method.category)));
---
<DocsLayout title="Every way to talk to LunaDash." section="api" summary="The dev branch exposes one owner-only Unix control socket, a versioned Settings API, the Quickshell shell object and Plugin SDK 2's synchronous C ABI. This page documents the contracts implemented by the current source tree.">
  <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#wire">Wire protocol</a><a href="#status">Status</a><a href="#methods">Methods</a><a href="#settings-api">Settings API</a><a href="#qml">QML</a><a href="#native">Native ABI</a></nav>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>This is a local session API, not HTTP.</strong> LunaDash binds a <code>QLocalServer</code> with user-only access. The website documents the API; it cannot control a running desktop.</p></div>

  <h2 id="wire">Wire protocol and ludashctl</h2>
  <p>Processes launched by LunaDash inherit <code>LUNADASH_CONTROL</code>. The client still accepts the historical <code>LUDASH_CONTROL</code>, then searches the runtime directory for one unambiguous <code>*-control</code> socket. Prefer <code>LUNADASH_CONTROL</code> in new code.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={'lunadashctl status\nlunadashctl workspace 1\nlunadashctl appearance \\'{"gap":16,"animations":true}\\'\nlunadashctl quit confirm'} />
  <p>The CLI sends one compact UTF-8 JSON object followed by a newline. <code>method</code> and <code>value</code> are strings, so structured payloads are JSON encoded inside <code>value</code>. The compositor accepts at most 65,536 request bytes, applies a three-second server timeout and returns one compact JSON object plus a newline.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="WIRE REQUEST" code={'{"method":"appearance","value":"{\\\\\"gap\\\\\":16}"}\\n'} />
  <p>Invalid JSON returns <code>{'{"error":"Invalid request"}'}</code>. An unsupported method/value returns <code>{'{"error":"Invalid command or value"}'}</code>. <code>lunadashctl</code> waits up to 1.5 seconds per socket read and refuses responses larger than 1 MiB.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="DIRECT SOCKET / PYTHON" code={'import json, os, socket\npath = os.environ.get("LUNADASH_CONTROL") or os.environ.get("LUDASH_CONTROL")\nrequest = {"method":"appearance","value":json.dumps({"gap":16})}\nwith socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX) as client:\n    client.settimeout(3)\n    client.connect(path)\n    client.sendall(json.dumps(request).encode() + b"\\\\n")\n    data = b""\n    while b"\\\\n" not in data:\n        data += client.recv(65536)\nresponse = json.loads(data.split(b"\\\\n", 1)[0])\nif "error" in response: raise RuntimeError(response["error"])\nprint(response)'} />

  <h2 id="status">Status is the discovery API</h2>
  <p>Use <code>status</code> to discover client ids, display modes, connection names, plugin ids, available power/session actions and layout actions instead of hard-coding host-specific values.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody>{statusFields.map(field => <tr><td class="api-method">{field.name}</td><td><code>{field.type}</code></td><td>{field.purpose}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <p>Each ordinary <code>status.clients[]</code> entry includes a positive session-local id, title, app id, icon, desktop id, X11 flag, workspace, geometry, focus/minimize/maximize/fullscreen/mapped flags and buffer/content sizes. Do not persist these ids across compositor restarts.</p>

  <h2 id="methods">Every control method</h2>
  <p>The tables are aligned with <code>WaylandCompositor::control()</code> on the dev branch. Examples use the CLI form; direct socket clients send the same method/value pair.</p>
  {categories.map(category => (
    <section>
      <h3>{category}</h3>
      <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Value</th><th>Behavior</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        {methods.filter(method => method.category === category).map(method => <tr><td class="api-method">{method.name}</td><td>{method.value}</td><td>{method.behavior}</td><td><code>{method.example}</code></td></tr>)}
      </tbody></table></div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h3>Network action payloads</h3>
  <p><code>network</code> accepts structured operations, never arbitrary <code>nmcli</code> text. Actions are <code>bluetooth-scan</code>, <code>network-reset</code>, <code>connection-reconnect</code>, <code>wifi-scan</code>, <code>wifi-connect</code>, <code>connection-up/down/delete</code>, <code>device-connect/disconnect</code>, <code>networking-enable</code>, <code>wifi-enable</code>, <code>connection-autoconnect</code>, <code>connection-ipv4-auto/manual</code>, <code>connection-ipv6-auto/disabled</code> and <code>connection-route-metric</code>.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="NETWORK EXAMPLES" code={'lunadashctl network \\'{"action":"wifi-scan"}\\'\nlunadashctl network \\'{"action":"wifi-connect","ssid":"Lab WiFi","password":"..."}\\'\nlunadashctl network \\'{"action":"networking-enable","enabled":true}\\'\nlunadashctl network \\'{"action":"connection-ipv4-manual","name":"Lab","address":"192.0.2.20/24","gateway":"192.0.2.1","dns":"1.1.1.1"}\\''} />

  <h3>Shortcut ids</h3>
  <p>Known actions are <code>focusLeft/Right/Up/Down</code>, <code>groupLeft/Right</code>, <code>reorderLeft/Right</code>, <code>expelWindow</code>, <code>centerColumn</code>, <code>widenColumn</code>, <code>narrowColumn</code>, <code>maximizeWindow</code>, <code>closeWindow</code>, <code>closeWindowAlternate</code>, <code>minimizeWindow</code>, <code>launchTerminal</code>, <code>launchTerminalAlternate</code>, <code>launchFiles</code>, <code>launchLauncher</code>, <code>screenshot</code>, plus <code>workspace1..10</code> and <code>moveToWorkspace1..10</code>. Values are <code>Disabled</code> or one key with modifiers; at least Meta or Alt is required.</p>

  <h2 id="settings-api">Settings API version 1</h2>
  <p><code>settings-describe</code> returns descriptors with <code>id</code>, <code>name</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>category</code>, normalized <code>schema</code>, current <code>values</code> and a SHA-256 <code>revision</code>. The revision hashes schema plus values for optimistic concurrency.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="TARGET ID FORMS" code={'builtin:<extension-target>\nplugin:<package-id>:<extension-target>\nmodule:<module-id>:<section>\nlayout:<active-window-template>'} />
  <CodeBlock label="PATCH FLOW" code={'# Read descriptors\nlunadashctl settings-describe\n\n# Send the selected target\\'s exact revision with a partial change\nlunadashctl settings-update \\'{"target":"plugin:org.example.motion:window-animation","revision":"<64-hex-sha256>","changes":{"duration":280}}\\''} />
  <p>If another editor changed the target, the patch fails with <code>Settings changed. Reload before applying this edit.</code>. Schemas can describe boolean, string, integer, number and bounded enum-array fields. Plugin schemas intentionally allow only toggle, select, number and slider controls.</p>

  <h2 id="qml">QML shell API</h2>
  <p>SDK 2 Quickshell plugins receive <code>shell</code>, validated <code>settings</code> and target-specific <code>context</code> before construction. Treat <code>shell.state</code> as read-only and perform mutations through control methods.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Member</th><th>Type</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead><tbody>{qmlApi.map(item => <tr><td class="api-method">{item.name}</td><td><code>{item.type}</code></td><td>{item.purpose}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <CodeBlock label="QML / SDK 2" code={'import QtQuick\n\nItem {\n    required property var shell\n    required property var settings\n    required property var context\n\n    Text { text: shell.tr("Focused") + ": " + shell.focusedTitle }\n    TapHandler { onTapped: shell.command("workspace", "1") }\n\n    Connections {\n        target: shell\n        function onCommandCompleted(method, result) {\n            if (method === "workspace" && result.error)\n                context.reportError(result.error)\n        }\n    }\n}'} />
  <p>Every visual context adds <code>target</code>, built-in <code>source</code>, <code>builtinSettings</code>, effective <code>mode</code> and <code>reportError(message)</code>. A plugin may expose <code>pluginReady: false</code>; a replacement does not hide the built-in until the loader is ready and <code>pluginReady</code> is true.</p>

  <h2 id="native">Native Plugin SDK 2 ABI</h2>
  <p>Native effects do not receive Qt or wlroots pointers. Hooks run synchronously on the compositor thread over UTF-8 JSON; do not block, retain host pointers, run nested event loops or create lifetime-escaping callbacks/background work.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="ABI" code={'#define LUDASH_PLUGIN_API_VERSION 2u\n\ntypedef struct ludash_plugin_api {\n  uint32_t struct_size;\n  uint32_t api_version;\n  const char *metadata_json;\n  int (*process)(const char *request, char *response, size_t capacity);\n} ludash_plugin_api;\n\nint ludash_plugin_process(const char *request, char *response, size_t capacity);\nconst ludash_plugin_api *ludash_plugin_entry_v2(void);\nint ludash_plugin_write_json(const char *json, char *response, size_t capacity);'} />
  <p>The SDK generates <code>ludash_plugin_entry_v2</code>, embeds the built manifest and produces the receipt. The loader checks struct size, API version 2, process pointer and equality between embedded and installed metadata.</p>
  <CodeBlock label="REQUEST ENVELOPE" code={'{\n  "target":"window-animation",\n  "mode":"replace",\n  "context":{},\n  "builtin":{"duration":220,"enterOffset":12,"focusOpacity":0.82,"exitScale":0.9,"easing":"outCubic"},\n  "current":{},\n  "settings":{"duration":280}\n}'} />
  <p><code>builtin</code> is always available. Replacement hooks get empty <code>current</code>; augment hooks receive the previous valid result. Return a complete JSON object and its byte length excluding NUL, or a negative value. The response buffer is 262,145 bytes. Invalid/oversized output quarantines the instance and preserves the built-in/previous result.</p>
  <p>The native targets are <code>window-animation</code>, <code>shell-animation</code>, <code>window-rules</code> and <code>window-layout</code>. Their contracts plus every visual target are in the <a href="../plugins/">Plugin SDK and registration guide</a>.</p>
  <div class="doc-callout"><p><strong>Trust boundary:</strong> Quickshell plugins run with user permissions and native effects run inside the compositor without a sandbox.</p></div>
</DocsLayout>
